{"id": "swebq0125", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "conservative", "audio_s": 2.18, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.3145, "eot_read_ms": 19, "reference_answer": "William Penn", "query": "where does name pennsylvania come from?", "transcript": "Where does name Pennsylvania come from?", "mode": "local", "answer": "The name Pennsylvania comes from a combination of two words. The first part, Penn, comes from William Penn. He was an Englishman who wanted to create a colony based on religious freedom and fair treatment of Native Americans. The second part, sylvania, is from the Latin word \"sylva,\" which means forest. So when you put them together, Pennsylvania means \"Penn's forest.\" It reflects both the land's natural beauty and its history with early settlers.", "answer_ms": 2141}
